{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>For a mockery.</b> This is שמץ and disgrace, for all the idolaters mock us over what our ancestors did with the calf. And one may answer them: every day they make defective things for idolatry and yet mock us. A parable — to a king who had a beautiful wife. Her maidservants would say: 'Our master the king will divorce you and take us as wives.' She says to them: 'Why?' They say to her: 'Because yesterday, when our master the king came from the market, he saw a little filth of soot on your hand and was disgusted with you.' She says to them: 'Fools! Would a beautiful woman like me, on account of a little smudge that I can wash away so that no trace remains — would he leave me? You, who are filthy with mud and the covering of pots all the time — he will take as wives?'"], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:31.065291377Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}